IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XIII -- Proxies (ss 147 to 154).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. The definitions of s 147 are rules of
-- this module and are named `... within s 147`. The "prescribed form", "prescribed circumstances" and
-- "prescribed" announcement are plain BOOLEAN inputs, because the regulations are not a source. The
-- "last business day" of s 148(4) and the "48 hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays" of s 148(5) are not
-- in the core's units of time, so the computed cut-off or the computed hours is a plain input (NOTES.md,
-- Needs from the core). Every offence states a ceiling, never an amount, in the shape declared in
-- cb3-nouns.l4. Dates: Part XIII holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XIII -- Proxies (ss 147 to 154)`

§§ `s 147 -- definitions`

-- "form of proxy": a written or printed form that, on completion and execution (in Quebec, signing) by or on behalf
-- of a shareholder, becomes a proxy.
-- src:1822 | form of proxy means a written or printed form that, on completion and execution or, in Quebec, on signing by or on behalf of a shareholder, becomes a proxy; (formulaire de procuration)
@ref CBCA s 147 form of proxy (src:1822)
GIVEN `it is a written or printed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on completion and execution, or in Quebec on signing, by or on behalf of a shareholder it becomes a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`form of proxy within s 147` MEANS
        `it is a written or printed form`
    AND `on completion and execution, or in Quebec on signing, by or on behalf of a shareholder it becomes a proxy`

-- "proxy": a completed and executed (in Quebec, signed) form of proxy by which a shareholder appoints a proxyholder
-- to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders.
-- src:1831 | proxy means a completed and executed or, in Quebec, signed form of proxy by means of which a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder’s behalf at a meeting of shareholders; (procuration)
@ref CBCA s 147 proxy (src:1831)
GIVEN `it is a form of proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is completed and executed, or in Quebec signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of it a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`proxy within s 147` MEANS
        `it is a form of proxy`
    AND `it is completed and executed, or in Quebec signed`
    AND `by means of it a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders`

-- "intermediary": a person who holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder, "and
-- includes" (a) to (g). "Includes" is read as extending the general description: a person in one of the listed kinds
-- is an intermediary whether or not the general description fits (fork F-147-includes). (g) is a kind of its own, with a
-- condition: a person who carries out similar functions AND holds a security registered in its name, or its nominee's,
-- for another who is not the registered holder. The caller states (d), the clearing agency's counterparties, as a fact.
-- src:1823 | intermediary means a person who holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security, and includes
-- src:1824 | (a) a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction;
-- src:1825 | (b) a securities depositary;
-- src:1826 | (c) a financial institution;
-- src:1827 | (d) in respect of a clearing agency, a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person, including another clearing agency, on whose behalf the clearing agency or its nominees hold securities of an issuer;
-- src:1828 | (e) a trustee or administrator of a self-administered retirement savings plan, retirement income fund, education savings plan or other similar self-administered savings or investment plan registered under the Income Tax Act;
-- src:1829 | (f) a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e); and
-- src:1830 | (g) a person who carries out functions similar to those carried out by individuals or entities referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e) and that holds a security registered in its name, or in the name of its nominee, on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security. (intermédiaire)
@ref CBCA s 147 intermediary (src:1823-1830)
GIVEN `the person holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a securities depositary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, in respect of a clearing agency, a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person on whose behalf the clearing agency or its nominees hold securities of an issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee or administrator of a self-administered retirement savings plan, retirement income fund, education savings plan or other similar self-administered savings or investment plan registered under the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries out functions similar to those carried out by individuals or entities referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a security registered in its name, or in the name of its nominee, on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`intermediary within s 147` MEANS
        `the person holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security`
    OR  `the person is a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction`
    OR  `the person is a securities depositary`
    OR  `the person is a financial institution`
    OR  `the person is, in respect of a clearing agency, a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person on whose behalf the clearing agency or its nominees hold securities of an issuer`
    OR  `the person is a trustee or administrator of a self-administered retirement savings plan, retirement income fund, education savings plan or other similar self-administered savings or investment plan registered under the Income Tax Act`
    OR  `the person is a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)`
    OR  (    `the person carries out functions similar to those carried out by individuals or entities referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)`
         AND `the person holds a security registered in its name, or in the name of its nominee, on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security`)

-- "solicit or solicitation": (a) "includes" four things; (b) "does not include" seven. The definition is open-ended
-- ("includes"), so an act that is in none of the four and none of the seven is NOT decided by this section. An act in
-- (b) is not a solicitation even if it is in (a). The rule returns JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (fork F-147-solicit).
-- src:1834 | (a) includes
-- src:1835 | (i) a request for a proxy whether or not accompanied by or included in a form of proxy,
-- src:1836 | (ii) a request to execute or not to execute or, in Quebec, to sign or not to sign a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy,
-- src:1837 | (iii) the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy, and
-- src:1838 | (iv) the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149; but
@ref CBCA s 147 solicit (a) (src:1834-1838)
GIVEN `it is a request for a proxy, whether or not accompanied by or included in a form of proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a request to execute or not to execute, or in Quebec to sign or not to sign, a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`act within the inclusions of solicit within s 147` MEANS
        `it is a request for a proxy, whether or not accompanied by or included in a form of proxy`
    OR  `it is a request to execute or not to execute, or in Quebec to sign or not to sign, a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy`
    OR  `it is the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy`
    OR  `it is the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149`

-- src:1839 | (b) does not include
-- src:1840 | (i) the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder,
-- src:1841 | (ii) the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy,
-- src:1842 | (iii) the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153,
-- src:1843 | (iv) a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which the person is the beneficial owner,
-- src:1844 | (v) a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons for that decision,
-- src:1845 | (vi) a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal under subsection 137(1.1), or
-- src:1846 | (vii) a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, that is made to shareholders, in any circumstances that may be prescribed; (sollicitation)
@ref CBCA s 147 solicit (b) (src:1839-1846)
GIVEN `it is the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which the person is the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons for that decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal under subsection 137(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, made to shareholders in circumstances that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`act within the exclusions of solicit within s 147` MEANS
        `it is the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder`
    OR  `it is the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy`
    OR  `it is the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153`
    OR  `it is a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which the person is the beneficial owner`
    OR  `it is a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons for that decision`
    OR  `it is a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal under subsection 137(1.1)`
    OR  `it is a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, made to shareholders in circumstances that may be prescribed`

-- src:1833 | solicit or solicitation
@ref CBCA s 147 solicit or solicitation (src:1833)
GIVEN `the act is within the inclusions of solicit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within the exclusions of solicit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`solicitation within s 147` MEANS
    IF `the act is within the exclusions of solicit`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the act is within the inclusions of solicit`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- "solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation": a solicitation by any person pursuant to a
-- resolution or instructions of, or with the acquiescence of, the directors or a committee of the directors.
-- src:1847 | solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation means a solicitation by any person pursuant to a resolution or instructions of, or with the acquiescence of, the directors or a committee of the directors. (sollicitation effectuée par la direction ou pour son compte)
@ref CBCA s 147 solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation (src:1847)
GIVEN `it is a solicitation by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is pursuant to a resolution or instructions of the directors or a committee of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with the acquiescence of the directors or a committee of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation within s 147` MEANS
        `it is a solicitation by any person`
    AND (    `it is pursuant to a resolution or instructions of the directors or a committee of the directors`
         OR  `it is with the acquiescence of the directors or a committee of the directors`)

§§ `s 148 -- proxies`

-- (1) A shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting may by means of a proxy appoint a proxyholder, or one or more
-- alternate proxyholders, who are not required to be shareholders, to attend and act at the meeting in the manner and to
-- the extent authorized by the proxy. The relation: the shareholder holds the power to appoint; the proxyholder takes the
-- authority the proxy confers. No input says the proxyholder is a shareholder: that is the point.
-- src:1849 | 148 (1) A shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders may by means of a proxy appoint a proxyholder or one or more alternate proxyholders who are not required to be shareholders, to attend and act at the meeting in the manner and to the extent authorized by the proxy and with the authority conferred by the proxy.
@ref CBCA s 148(1) (src:1849)
GIVEN `the person appointing is a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is by means of a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder may appoint a proxyholder within s 148(1)` MEANS
        `the person appointing is a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting`
    AND `the appointment is by means of a proxy`

-- (2) A proxy shall be executed (in Quebec, signed) by the shareholder or by the shareholder's personal representative
-- authorized in writing.
-- src:1851 | (2) A proxy shall be executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder or by the shareholder’s personal representative authorized in writing.
@ref CBCA s 148(2) (src:1851)
GIVEN `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder's personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that personal representative is authorized in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proxy is executed as s 148(2) requires within s 148(2)` MEANS
        `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder`
    OR  (    `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder's personal representative`
         AND `that personal representative is authorized in writing`)

-- (3) A proxy is valid only at the meeting in respect of which it is given or any adjournment of it.
-- src:1853 | (3) A proxy is valid only at the meeting in respect of which it is given or any adjournment thereof.
@ref CBCA s 148(3) (src:1853)
GIVEN `the meeting is the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an adjournment of the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proxy is valid at the meeting within s 148(3)` MEANS
        `the meeting is the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given`
    OR  `the meeting is an adjournment of the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given`

-- (4) A shareholder may revoke a proxy (a) by depositing an instrument or act in writing executed (in Quebec, signed) by the
-- shareholder or the shareholder's authorized personal representative (i) at the registered office at any time up to and
-- including the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or an adjournment, at which the proxy is to be used, or
-- (ii) with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting or an adjournment; or (b) in any other manner permitted by
-- law. The last business day is a plain DATE (business days are not in the core's units).
-- src:1855 | (4) A shareholder may revoke a proxy
-- src:1856 | (a) by depositing an instrument or act in writing executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder or by the shareholder’s personal representative authorized in writing
-- src:1857 | (i) at the registered office of the corporation at any time up to and including the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or an adjournment thereof, at which the proxy is to be used, or
-- src:1858 | (ii) with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting or an adjournment thereof; or
-- src:1859 | (b) in any other manner permitted by law.
@ref CBCA s 148(4) (src:1855-1859)
GIVEN `the instrument or act in writing is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder or by the shareholder's personal representative authorized in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the instrument or act was deposited at the registered office of the corporation, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or an adjournment of it, at which the proxy is to be used` IS A DATE
      `the instrument or act was deposited with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting or an adjournment of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder revoked the proxy in any other manner permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proxy is revoked within s 148(4)` MEANS
        `the shareholder revoked the proxy in any other manner permitted by law`
    OR  (    `the instrument or act in writing is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder or by the shareholder's personal representative authorized in writing`
         AND (    (CONSIDER `the date the instrument or act was deposited at the registered office of the corporation, if it was`
                   WHEN JUST deposited THEN deposited AT MOST `the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or an adjournment of it, at which the proxy is to be used`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
              OR  `the instrument or act was deposited with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting or an adjournment of it`))

-- (5) The directors may specify in a notice calling a meeting a time not more than 48 hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays,
-- before the meeting or adjournment before which time proxies to be used at the meeting must be deposited with the corporation
-- or its agent or mandatary. The hours are counted by the caller, Saturdays and holidays already excluded.
-- src:1861 | (5) The directors may specify in a notice calling a meeting of shareholders a time not more than 48 hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment before which time proxies to be used at the meeting must be deposited with the corporation or its agent or mandatary.
@ref CBCA s 148(5) (src:1861)
GIVEN `the time is specified in a notice calling the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment at which the time falls` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may specify the time for depositing proxies within s 148(5)` MEANS
        `the time is specified in a notice calling the meeting`
    AND `the hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment at which the time falls` AT MOST 48

§§ `s 149 -- mandatory solicitation`

-- (2) The management is not required to send a form of proxy under (1) if the corporation (a) is not a distributing
-- corporation and (b) has fifty or fewer shareholders entitled to vote at a meeting, two or more joint holders being counted
-- as one shareholder (the caller counts them so).
-- src:1865 | (2) The management of the corporation is not required to send a form of proxy under subsection (1) if it
-- src:1866 | (a) is not a distributing corporation; and
-- src:1867 | (b) has fifty or fewer shareholders entitled to vote at a meeting, two or more joint holders being counted as one shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 149(2) (src:1865-1867)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`management is not required to send a form of proxy within s 149(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)
    AND `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` AT MOST 50

-- (1) Subject to (2), the management shall, concurrently with giving notice of a meeting, send a form of proxy in prescribed
-- form to each shareholder entitled to receive notice. The relation: the shareholders entitled to notice are owed the form;
-- the management owes it.
-- src:1863 | 149 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the management of a corporation shall, concurrently with giving notice of a meeting of shareholders, send a form of proxy in prescribed form to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 149(1) (src:1863)
GIVEN `management is not required to send a form of proxy under subsection 149(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)` MEANS
    (NOT `management is not required to send a form of proxy under subsection 149(2)`)

@ref CBCA s 149(1) (src:1863)
GIVEN `management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the form of proxy was sent` IS A DATE
      `the form of proxy is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sent to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to send a form of proxy is met within s 149(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)`)
    OR  (    `the date the form of proxy was sent` EQUALS `the date the notice of the meeting was given`
         AND `the form of proxy is in the prescribed form`
         AND `it was sent to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting`)

-- (3) If the management fails to comply without reasonable cause with (1), the corporation is guilty of an offence and liable on
-- summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars: no imprisonment ceiling (a corporation is not imprisoned,
-- and the section states none, so NOTHING).
-- src:1869 | (3) If the management of a corporation fails to comply, without reasonable cause, with subsection (1), the corporation is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 149(3) (src:1869)
GIVEN `management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management failed to comply with subsection 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 149(3)` MEANS
        `management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)`
    AND `the management failed to comply with subsection 149(1)`
    AND `the failure was without reasonable cause`

@ref CBCA s 149(3) (src:1869)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 149(3)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

-- (4) Where the corporation commits an offence under (3), any director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or
-- acquiesced is a party to and guilty of the offence, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted: what is
-- required is that the offence was committed, not that anyone was convicted of it. Fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment
-- not exceeding six months, or both.
-- src:1871 | (4) Where a corporation commits an offence under subsection (3), any director or officer of the corporation who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 149(4) (src:1871)
GIVEN `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 149(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 149(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 149(3)`
    AND `the person is a director or officer of the corporation`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

@ref CBCA s 149(4) (src:1871)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 149(4)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 150 -- soliciting proxies`

-- (1) A person shall not solicit proxies unless (a) for a solicitation by or on behalf of the management, a management proxy
-- circular in prescribed form, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting, or (b) for any
-- other solicitation, a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation, is sent to the
-- auditor, to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited, to each director and, if (b) applies, to the corporation.
-- The relation: those recipients are owed the circular; the person soliciting owes it.
-- src:1873 | 150 (1) A person shall not solicit proxies unless
-- src:1874 | (a) in the case of solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation, a management proxy circular in prescribed form, either as an appendix to or as a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting, or
-- src:1875 | (b) in the case of any other solicitation, a dissident’s proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation
-- src:1876 | is sent to the auditor of the corporation, to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited, to each director and, if paragraph (b) applies, to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 150(1) (src:1873-1876)
GIVEN `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular is sent to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the circular required by s 150(1) is sent within s 150(1)` MEANS
        (IF `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation`
         THEN `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting`
         ELSE `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent`)
    AND `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation`
    AND `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited`
    AND `the circular is sent to each director`
    AND (    `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation`
         OR  `the circular is sent to the corporation`)

-- (1.1), (1.2) Despite (1), a person other than the management may solicit proxies without sending a dissident's proxy
-- circular if the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited is fifteen or fewer, joint holders counted as one
-- (the caller counts them so); or if the solicitation is, in the prescribed circumstances, conveyed by public broadcast, speech
-- or publication. The management has no such exception.
-- src:1878 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), a person may solicit proxies, other than by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, without sending a dissident’s proxy circular, if the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited is fifteen or fewer, two or more joint holders being counted as one shareholder.
-- src:1879 | Exception — solicitation by public broadcast
-- src:1880 | (1.2) Despite subsection (1), a person may solicit proxies, other than by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, without sending a dissident’s proxy circular if the solicitation is, in the prescribed circumstances, conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication.
@ref CBCA s 150(1.1), (1.2) (src:1878-1880)
GIVEN `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular required by s 150(1) is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER
      `the solicitation is conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may solicit proxies within s 150(1), (1.1) and (1.2)` MEANS
        `the circular required by s 150(1) is sent`
    OR  (    (NOT `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation`)
         AND (    `the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited, joint holders counted as one` AT MOST 15
              OR  `the solicitation is conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances`))

-- (2) A person required to send a circular shall send concurrently a copy to the Director, with a statement in prescribed form,
-- the form of proxy, any other documents for use in connection with the meeting and, for a management proxy circular, a copy of
-- the notice of the meeting. "Concurrently" is the same day as the circular.
-- src:1882 | (2) A person required to send a management proxy circular or dissident’s proxy circular shall send concurrently a copy of it to the Director together with a statement in prescribed form, the form of proxy, any other documents for use in connection with the meeting and, in the case of a management proxy circular, a copy of the notice of meeting.
@ref CBCA s 150(2) (src:1882)
GIVEN `the person is required to send a management proxy circular or a dissident's proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circular is a management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the circular was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy was sent to the Director` IS A DATE
      `the copy is sent with a statement in prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is sent with the form of proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is sent with any other documents for use in connection with the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is sent with a copy of the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the copy to the Director complies with s 150(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the person is required to send a management proxy circular or a dissident's proxy circular`)
    OR  (    `the date the copy was sent to the Director` EQUALS `the date the circular was sent`
         AND `the copy is sent with a statement in prescribed form`
         AND `the copy is sent with the form of proxy`
         AND `the copy is sent with any other documents for use in connection with the meeting`
         AND (    (NOT `the circular is a management proxy circular`)
              OR  `the copy is sent with a copy of the notice of the meeting`))

-- (3) A person who fails to comply with (1) and (2) is guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding six months, or both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted. "(1) and (2)" is read as either one
-- (fork F-150-3).
-- src:1884 | (3) A person who fails to comply with subsections (1) and (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 150(3) (src:1884)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with subsection 150(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with subsection 150(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is guilty of an offence within s 150(3)` MEANS
        `the person failed to comply with subsection 150(1)`
    OR  `the person failed to comply with subsection 150(2)`

@ref CBCA s 150(3) (src:1884)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 150(3)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- (4) Where a body corporate commits an offence under (3), a director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or
-- acquiesced is a party to and guilty of it, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
-- src:1886 | (4) Where a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (3), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 150(4) (src:1886)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 150(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director or officer of a body corporate is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 150(4)` MEANS
        `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 150(3)`
    AND `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

@ref CBCA s 150(4) (src:1886)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 150(4)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 151 -- exemption by the Director`

-- (1) On the application of an interested person, the Director may exempt the person, on any terms the Director thinks fit, from
-- any requirement of s 149, s 150(1) or s 153(1); the exemption may have retroactive effect. The rule says who may be exempted
-- and from what; whether the Director does so is the Director's discretion and is not decided. The relation: the interested
-- person holds the power to apply; the Director holds the power to exempt.
-- src:1888 | 151 (1) On the application of an interested person, the Director may exempt the person, on any terms that the Director thinks fit, from any of the requirements of section 149 or subsection 150(1) or 153(1). The exemption may have retroactive effect.
@ref CBCA s 151(1) (src:1888)
GIVEN `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is a requirement of section 149, subsection 150(1) or subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may exempt the person within s 151(1)` MEANS
        `the applicant is an interested person`
    AND `the requirement is a requirement of section 149, subsection 150(1) or subsection 153(1)`

@ref CBCA s 151(1) (src:1888)
GIVEN `the Director has granted an exemption under subsection 151(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exemption may have retroactive effect within s 151(1)` MEANS
    `the Director has granted an exemption under subsection 151(1)`

§§ `s 152 -- the proxyholder`

-- (1) A person who solicits a proxy and is appointed proxyholder shall attend in person or cause an alternate proxyholder to
-- attend the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given and comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed
-- them. The relation: the appointing shareholder holds the claim; the proxyholder bears the duty.
-- src:1891 | 152 (1) A person who solicits a proxy and is appointed proxyholder shall attend in person or cause an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given and comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed him.
@ref CBCA s 152(1) (src:1891)
GIVEN `the person solicits a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proxyholder must attend and comply with the directions within s 152(1)` MEANS
        `the person solicits a proxy`
    AND `the person is appointed proxyholder`

@ref CBCA s 152(1) (src:1891)
GIVEN `the proxyholder must attend and comply with the directions within s 152(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attends the meeting in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the directions of the shareholder who appointed them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to attend and comply with the directions is met within s 152(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the proxyholder must attend and comply with the directions within s 152(1)`)
    OR  (    (    `the person attends the meeting in person`
              OR  `the person causes an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting`)
         AND `the person complies with the directions of the shareholder who appointed them`)

-- (2) A proxyholder or alternate has the same rights as the shareholder who appointed them to speak at the meeting on any matter,
-- to vote by ballot, and, except where they have conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder, to vote by a show of
-- hands. Three rules, one for each right.
-- src:1893 | (2) A proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder has the same rights as the shareholder by whom they were appointed to speak at a meeting of shareholders in respect of any matter, to vote by way of ballot at the meeting and, except where a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder has conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder, to vote at such a meeting in respect of any matter by way of any show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 152(2) (src:1893)
GIVEN `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to speak within s 152(2)` MEANS
    `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

@ref CBCA s 152(2) (src:1893)
GIVEN `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to vote by ballot within s 152(2)` MEANS
    `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

@ref CBCA s 152(2) (src:1893)
GIVEN `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to vote by a show of hands within s 152(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`
    AND (NOT `the person has conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder`)

-- (3) Despite (1) and (2), if the chairperson declares to the meeting that, on a ballot, the votes attached to shares represented
-- by proxy that are required to be voted against what to the chairperson's knowledge will be the decision of the meeting on a
-- matter or group of matters are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot by shareholders
-- personally or through proxy, then, unless a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot, (a) the chairperson may conduct the
-- vote on that matter or group by a show of hands, and (b) a proxyholder or alternate may vote on it by a show of hands. The
-- fraction is the votes required to be voted against over all the votes that might be cast; the caller divides.
-- src:1895 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if the chairperson of a meeting of shareholders declares to the meeting that, if a ballot is conducted, the total number of votes attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy required to be voted against what to the knowledge of the chairperson will be the decision of the meeting in relation to any matter or group of matters is less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast by shareholders personally or through proxy at the meeting on the ballot, unless a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot,
-- src:1896 | (a) the chairperson may conduct the vote in respect of that matter or group of matters by a show of hands; and
-- src:1897 | (b) a proxyholder or alternate proxyholder may vote in respect of that matter or group of matters by a show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 152(3) (src:1895-1897)
GIVEN `the chairperson declares to the meeting that the votes attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against the decision of the meeting are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot that are attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against what to the knowledge of the chairperson will be the decision of the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(a)` MEANS
        `the chairperson declares to the meeting that the votes attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against the decision of the meeting are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot`
    AND `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot that are attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against what to the knowledge of the chairperson will be the decision of the meeting` LESS THAN (5%)
    AND (NOT `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot`)

@ref CBCA s 152(3)(b) (src:1897)
GIVEN `the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proxyholder may vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(b)` MEANS
        `the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(a)`
    AND `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

-- (4) A proxyholder or alternate who without reasonable cause fails to comply with the shareholder's directions under the section
-- is guilty of an offence: fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
-- src:1899 | (4) A proxyholder or alternate proxyholder who without reasonable cause fails to comply with the directions of a shareholder under this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 152(4) (src:1899)
GIVEN `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with the directions of a shareholder under s 152` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proxyholder is guilty of an offence within s 152(4)` MEANS
        `the person is a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`
    AND `the person failed to comply with the directions of a shareholder under s 152`
    AND `the failure was without reasonable cause`

@ref CBCA s 152(4) (src:1899)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 152(4)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 153 -- the intermediary`

-- (1) Shares registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee and not beneficially owned by the intermediary must not
-- be voted unless the intermediary, without delay after receiving the notice of the meeting, financial statements, circulars and
-- other documents (other than the form of proxy), sends a copy of each to the beneficial owner and, except where it has received
-- written voting instructions, a written request for instructions. "Without delay" is the caller's judgment.
-- The relation: the beneficial owner holds the claim to the documents and the request; the intermediary the duty.
-- src:1901 | 153 (1) Shares of a corporation that are registered in the name of an intermediary or their nominee and not beneficially owned by the intermediary must not be voted unless the intermediary, without delay after receipt of the notice of the meeting, financial statements, management proxy circular, dissident’s proxy circular and any other documents other than the form of proxy sent to shareholders by or on behalf of any person for use in connection with the meeting, sends a copy of the document to the beneficial owner and, except when the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner, a written request for such instructions.
@ref CBCA s 153(1) (src:1901)
GIVEN `the shares are registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares must not be voted unless s 153(1) is met within s 153(1)` MEANS
        `the shares are registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee`
    AND `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary`

@ref CBCA s 153(1) (src:1901)
GIVEN `the shares must not be voted unless s 153(1) is met within s 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary sent a copy of each document to the beneficial owner without delay after receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary sent the beneficial owner a written request for voting instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares may be voted within s 153(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the shares must not be voted unless s 153(1) is met within s 153(1)`)
    OR  (    `the intermediary sent a copy of each document to the beneficial owner without delay after receiving it`
         AND (    `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`
              OR  `the intermediary sent the beneficial owner a written request for voting instructions`))

-- (2) An intermediary, or a proxyholder it appoints, may not vote shares it does not beneficially own that are registered in its
-- name or its nominee's unless it receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner.
-- src:1903 | (2) An intermediary, or a proxyholder appointed by an intermediary, may not vote shares that the intermediary does not beneficially own and that are registered in the name of the intermediary or in the name of a nominee of the intermediary unless the intermediary or proxyholder, as the case may be, receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner.
@ref CBCA s 153(2) (src:1903)
GIVEN `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are registered in the name of the intermediary or in the name of a nominee of the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary or the proxyholder receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`voting is prohibited within s 153(2)` MEANS
        `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary`
    AND `the shares are registered in the name of the intermediary or in the name of a nominee of the intermediary`
    AND (NOT `the intermediary or the proxyholder receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`)

-- (3) A person by or on behalf of whom a solicitation is made shall provide, at the intermediary's request, without delay and at
-- the person's expense, the necessary number of copies of the documents of (1), other than copies of the document requesting
-- voting instructions.
-- src:1905 | (3) A person by or on behalf of whom a solicitation is made shall provide, at the request of an intermediary, without delay, to the intermediary at the person’s expense the necessary number of copies of the documents referred to in subsection (1), other than copies of the document requesting voting instructions.
@ref CBCA s 153(3) (src:1905)
GIVEN `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must provide copies to the intermediary within s 153(3)` MEANS
        `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of the person`
    AND `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)`

@ref CBCA s 153(3) (src:1905)
GIVEN `the person must provide copies to the intermediary within s 153(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides the necessary number of copies without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides them at the person's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to provide copies is met within s 153(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the person must provide copies to the intermediary within s 153(3)`)
    OR  (    `the person provides the necessary number of copies without delay`
         AND `the person provides them at the person's expense`)

-- (4) An intermediary shall vote, or appoint a proxyholder to vote, the shares referred to in (1) in accordance with any written
-- voting instructions received from the beneficial owner.
-- src:1907 | (4) An intermediary shall vote or appoint a proxyholder to vote any shares referred to in subsection (1) in accordance with any written voting instructions received from the beneficial owner.
@ref CBCA s 153(4) (src:1907)
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the intermediary must vote in accordance with the instructions within s 153(4)` MEANS
        `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)`
    AND `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`

@ref CBCA s 153(4) (src:1907)
GIVEN `the intermediary must vote in accordance with the instructions within s 153(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary votes the shares in accordance with the instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary appoints a proxyholder to vote the shares in accordance with the instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to vote in accordance with the instructions is met within s 153(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the intermediary must vote in accordance with the instructions within s 153(4)`)
    OR  `the intermediary votes the shares in accordance with the instructions`
    OR  `the intermediary appoints a proxyholder to vote the shares in accordance with the instructions`

-- (5) If a beneficial owner so requests and provides the intermediary with appropriate documentation, the intermediary must
-- appoint the beneficial owner, or a nominee of theirs, as proxyholder. "Appropriate" documentation is the caller's judgment.
-- src:1909 | (5) If a beneficial owner so requests and provides an intermediary with appropriate documentation, the intermediary must appoint the beneficial owner or a nominee of the beneficial owner as proxyholder.
@ref CBCA s 153(5) (src:1909)
GIVEN `the beneficial owner requests that the beneficial owner or a nominee be appointed proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficial owner provides the intermediary with appropriate documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the intermediary must appoint the beneficial owner or a nominee as proxyholder within s 153(5)` MEANS
        `the beneficial owner requests that the beneficial owner or a nominee be appointed proxyholder`
    AND `the beneficial owner provides the intermediary with appropriate documentation`

-- (6) An intermediary's failure to comply with the section does not render void any meeting of shareholders or any action taken
-- at it. The rule answers whether the failure makes a meeting or action void; the answer is no.
-- src:1911 | (6) The failure of an intermediary to comply with this section does not render void any meeting of shareholders or any action taken at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 153(6) (src:1911)
GIVEN `an intermediary failed to comply with section 153` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the failure renders a meeting or an action void within s 153(6)` MEANS
    FALSE

-- (7) Nothing in the section gives an intermediary the right to vote shares it is otherwise prohibited from voting. The section
-- gives no right in any case, so the answer is JUST FALSE where the intermediary is otherwise prohibited and NOTHING where it
-- is not (whether it may then vote is for the law outside the section).
-- src:1913 | (7) Nothing in this section gives an intermediary the right to vote shares that the intermediary is otherwise prohibited from voting.
@ref CBCA s 153(7) (src:1913)
GIVEN `the intermediary is otherwise prohibited from voting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153 gives the intermediary the right to vote within s 153(7)` MEANS
    IF `the intermediary is otherwise prohibited from voting the shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (8) An intermediary who knowingly fails to comply with the section is guilty of an offence: fine not exceeding $5,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both. (9) If an intermediary that is a body corporate commits it, a director or
-- officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced is a party to and guilty of it, whether or not the body corporate has
-- been prosecuted or convicted.
-- src:1915 | (8) An intermediary who knowingly fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 153(8) (src:1915)
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary failed to comply with section 153` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intermediary knew that it failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an intermediary is guilty of an offence within s 153(8)` MEANS
        `the person is an intermediary`
    AND `the intermediary failed to comply with section 153`
    AND `the intermediary knew that it failed to comply`

@ref CBCA s 153(8) (src:1915)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 153(8)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- src:1917 | (9) If an intermediary that is a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (8), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 153(9) (src:1917)
GIVEN `the intermediary is a body corporate and commits an offence under subsection 153(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director or officer of an intermediary is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 153(9)` MEANS
        `the intermediary is a body corporate and commits an offence under subsection 153(8)`
    AND `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

@ref CBCA s 153(9) (src:1917)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 153(9)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 154 -- restraining order`

-- (1) If a form of proxy, management proxy circular or dissident's proxy circular contains an untrue statement of a material
-- fact, or omits a material fact required in it or necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the circumstances, an
-- interested person or the Director may apply to a court, and the court may make any order it thinks fit, including orders of
-- the kinds listed. The rule says who may apply and on what ground; the order is the court's. "Material" is the caller's judgment.
-- src:1919 | 154 (1) If a form of proxy, management proxy circular or dissident’s proxy circular contains an untrue statement of a material fact or omits to state a material fact required therein or necessary to make a statement contained therein not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made, an interested person or the Director may apply to a court and the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref CBCA s 154(1) (src:1919)
GIVEN `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document omits to state a material fact required in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may apply to the court within s 154(1)` MEANS
        (    `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact`
         OR  `the document omits to state a material fact required in it`
         OR  `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made`)
    AND (    `the applicant is an interested person`
         OR  `the applicant is the Director`)

-- src:1920 | (a) an order restraining the solicitation, the holding of the meeting, or any person from implementing or acting on any resolution passed at the meeting to which the form of proxy, management proxy circular or dissident’s proxy circular relates;
-- src:1921 | (b) an order requiring correction of any form of proxy or proxy circular and a further solicitation; and
-- src:1922 | (c) an order adjourning the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 154(1) (src:1920-1922)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 154(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an order restraining the solicitation, the holding of the meeting, or any person from implementing or acting on any resolution passed at the meeting`
    `an order requiring correction of any form of proxy or proxy circular and a further solicitation`
    `an order adjourning the meeting`
    `any other order the court thinks fit`

@ref CBCA s 154(1) (src:1919-1922)
GIVEN `a person may apply to the court under subsection 154(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of order under s 154(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order of a kind within s 154(1)` MEANS
    `a person may apply to the court under subsection 154(1)`

-- (2) An applicant under the section shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and
-- to be heard in person or by counsel.
-- src:1924 | (2) An applicant under this section shall give to the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and to be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 154(2) (src:1924)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice within s 154(2)` MEANS
    `the person is an applicant under section 154`

@ref CBCA s 154(2) (src:1924)
GIVEN `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 154(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant gave the Director notice of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to give the Director notice is met within s 154(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 154(2)`)
    OR  `the applicant gave the Director notice of the application`

@ref CBCA s 154(2) (src:1924)
GIVEN `the application is under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 154(2)` MEANS
    `the application is under section 154`
